tasks.brief:
Implementation constraints: Edit src/static/style.css. Add exactly two CSS rule groups. No other edits to this file. No JavaScript, no async, no external libraries.

Behavioral specification: Add the following CSS rules exactly:

.search-hit-nav {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin: 0.15rem 0.75rem 0.4rem;
  color: var(--sidebar-text);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
}
.search-hit-nav[hidden] {
  display: none;
}
.hit-nav-btn {
  background: transparent;
  border: 1px solid var(--sidebar-border);
  color: var(--sidebar-text);
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
  padding: 0 0.35rem;
  font-size: 0.7rem;
}
mark.search-hit.current {
  background: var(--accent-hover);
  outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
}

Acceptance condition: src/static/style.css contains all four CSS rules with the exact selectors and properties listed above.

Implementation constraints: Edit src/static/threads.js. Add two module-level variables (hitElements array init [], hitIndex number init 0). Modify highlightSearchHits() to clear hitElements on empty query, collect mark.search-hit elements into hitElements at end, set hitIndex to 0, call updateHitNav(). Remove existing scroll-to-first behavior. Add new functions updateHitNav() and gotoHit(delta). Add click listeners for search-prev-btn and search-next-btn. No other edits. No async, no external libraries.

Behavioral specification: 1) Module-level: let hitElements = []; let hitIndex = 0; 2) In highlightSearchHits(): if query is empty, hitElements = []; return; at end, hitElements = document.querySelectorAll('mark.search-hit'); hitIndex = 0; updateHitNav(); remove existing scrollIntoView call. 3) updateHitNav(): const nav = document.querySelector('.search-hit-nav'); if (!nav) return; if (hitElements.length === 0) { nav.hidden = true; return; } nav.hidden = false; const countSpan = document.querySelector('[data-testid="search-hit-count"]'); if (countSpan) countSpan.textContent = hitElements.length ? (hitIndex + 1) + '/' + hitElements.length : '0/0'; hitElements.forEach(el => el.classList.remove('current')); if (hitElements.length > 0) { hitElements[hitIndex].classList.add('current'); hitElements[hitIndex].scrollIntoView({ block: 'center' }); } 4) gotoHit(delta): if (hitElements.length === 0) return; hitIndex = (hitIndex + delta % hitElements.length + hitElements.length) % hitElements.length; updateHitNav(); 5) Wiring: next to existing thread-search listener, add: const prevBtn = document.querySelector('[data-testid="search-prev-btn"]'); const nextBtn = document.querySelector('[data-testid="search-next-btn"]'); if (prevBtn) prevBtn.addEventListener('click', () => gotoHit(-1)); if (nextBtn) nextBtn.addEventListener('click', () => gotoHit(1));

Acceptance condition: Typing in search highlights hits; prev/next buttons cycle through hits with wrapping; count span shows current/total; current hit is highlighted with CSS class.
